SUMMARY:Pisgah Forest/Brevard NC—Estatoe Trail River Walk—5 KM/3 mi. o
 r 10 KM/6 mi. Walk
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nThis is a free walk in Tr
 ansylvania County. We will amble along shaded pathways beside the Davidson
  River which includes a portion of the Estatoe Trail\, used by the Cheroke
 e as a trade route between western NC and SC. There will be a nature trail
  and quiet\, peaceful scenes. It goes through forests and through a campgr
 ound.\n\nThis is a beginner walk\, little elevation change\, on well-groom
 ed trails. Trails are hard pack with some areas having exposed roots. The 
 trail itself is almost entirely flat. Tennis shoes are fine\, though some 
 might want hiking boots. Walking sticks are not needed\, though some might
  choose to bring them\; I plan to use one stick.\n\nPlease bring **plenty 
 of water** and a protein snack. Dress for the temperature and weather\; co
 nsider a hat and sunscreen. Dogs are welcome.\n\nWe will be walking with t
 he Asheville Amblers Walking Club\, AARP\, Stryder\, and perhaps some othe
 rs. Registration is in the Lowe's\, 119 Ecusta Road\, Brevard\, parking lo
 t at 8:30 a.m.\, with step-off at 9:00. There are bathrooms inside Lowe's\
 , but none on the trail. There are 5 KM and 10 KM guided walk options. The
  pace of the 5 KM group is a little slower\, the pace of the 10 KM group a
  little faster.\n\nThere are several eating places in the immediate area\,
  but the most important is Dolly's Ice Cream\, a place never to be missed.
 \n\nSee you there.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/315376705/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260622T233957Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260622T233957Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
